  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 308 AM EDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nAn upper ridge extends from the SE states into the southern/ \ncentral Lakes. Multiple shortwaves are lifting into this ridge, \nincluding waves in western MN and eastern KS. These are \ncontributing to the broad area of clouds and sporadic (mostly \nlight) precip to our w, trying to work east. 1034mb surface high\npressure is just north of Georgian Bay, and the low levels in \nour neck of the north woods are on the dry side. Precip is \neroding somewhat as it works east, though not completely; we've\nhad a few sprinkles here at APX proper since 11 pm. \n\nAnother upstream area of somewhat better light precip is\npassing between MQT and GRB. This should also weaken as it\nmoves east, but some sprinkles and perhaps -SHRA are possible\nearly this morning, especially in the broader Straits area.\nAnother uptick in warm/moist advection could produce a slight \nchance for afternoon/evening showers, especially in eastern \nupper MI. Otherwise, more clouds than sun across northern MI \ntoday, with highs from the mid 40s at ANJ to pushing 60f at MBL.\n\nUpper flow in the Conus tends to deamplify this week. We are\ninitially seeing wsw flow aloft, but that becomes more zonal\nlater on. Return flow will amp up later on Wednesday, as high\npressure moves east, and ahead of a cold front advancing into\nMN. With moisture return initially limited, Wednesday looks\na potentially rather warm day (for late October). Should be a\npartly to mostly sunny day, with highs from the low-mid 60s\nnorth, to near 70f in most on northern lower MI. We could flirt\nwith some record highs, in particular at our more northerly\nclimate sites (Soo/PLN/GLR).\n\nA narrow zone of better moisture return will finally accompany\nthe surface cold front across northern MI Wed night into Thu.\nShowers are likely to widespread in nw lower and eastern upper\nMI late Wed night, and perhaps a rumble of thunder is possible,\nespecially west of TVC. Precip chances do dwindle somewhat with\neastern extent late Wed night into Thu. Shower chances exit by \nThu evening. Still a potentially mild/warm day Thu, especially\nin ne lower MI (mid 60s APN-HTL, near 70f near Saginaw Bay). \n\nAfter this, trailing high pressure marches from the lee of the\nCanadian Rockies to eventually the Great Lakes and points east.\nSo quieter and still mild wx to end the weak. We will try to get\nsome return flow this weekend trailing the high, but it will be\nlimited/slow initially, and some surface ridging will still be\nhanging on in the northern lakes. So pops are limited to slight\nchance in western areas for Saturday and trick-or-treating\nactivities into the evening. Chances for rain looks somewhat\nhigher Sunday, and for Monday night-Tuesday.",
